{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>If there be a prophet among you, HaShem —</b> This response is to what they said: ״Has He not spoken also with us?״ That is: the speech with which I speak with you and with the other prophets is not comparable to the speech with which I speak with Moses. With another prophet, בחלום אדבר בו — like a person who sees a dream and requires an interpretation. במראה אליו אתודע — like a person who sees his reflection in a mirror and does not see the actual thing — that is, by way of allegory I speak with them, as it is written: ״שכב על צדך השמאלית״, and similarly in Daniel it is written: ״אני ראיתי ולא אבין״, and so too many others."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:49.485408443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}